d38880b7 (1 1790696747454 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (set "8pniyrtk.8r" src "`theourgia-mcp --store <path>` speaks MCP `2025-11-25` over stdio. Register it once:\n\n```\nclaude mcp add theourgia -- theourgia-mcp --store /path/to/store --actor <name> --writer <name>\n```\n\nOr in a client's JSON configuration:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"theourgia\": {\n      \"command\": \"theourgia-mcp\",\n      \"args\": [\"--store\", \"/path/to/store\", \"--actor\", \"<name>\", \"--writer\", \"<name>\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nOne tool per verb, named `theourgia_<verb>`, each taking `{\"argv\": [...]}` with the command line's own arguments as an array of strings. The shell asks the core what verbs exist on every call, so a verb added to a newer build appears without restarting the server.\n\nThe core's answer arrives as S-expression text, byte for byte. A core refusal is a successful tool result, not a JSON-RPC error: `(error unknown-id ...)` is the store's answer to the question asked, delivered with `isError: false`. Only the shell's own failures use the JSON-RPC error channel: a frame it could not parse, a frame past the size limit, or a connection that was made and then lost. A lost connection says the request may have been carried out, because it may have been; a request that reached nobody says it was not.\n\n`eval` is not offered as a tool; it is available only through the local CLI. `init` is not offered either, because the store must exist before the MCP server starts."))
fc9854c9 (2 1790696777237 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (set "8pniyrtk.8s" src "A writer id is held by one live agent at a time. The id is derived from the actor name by default, or set explicitly with `THEOURGIA_WRITER` in the environment or `--writer` on the command line; the MCP shell's initialize response names which writer the session is using.\n\nA later session may bind the same id and carry on with its drafts, but two agents writing under one id at the same moment overwrite each other silently. There is no lock and no refusal: the rule is stated here, and the failure it prevents is silent. A host giving several agents the same actor must give each its own `--writer`."))
e119bbd4 (3 1790696784877 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "One store per machine") (src . "One store per project or per person, on one machine. The machine registry records which stores are where. Moving a store to another machine requires adopt, which transfers its entry in the registry. Two machines writing one store is not supported.") (parent . "8pniyrtk.n") (ord . 12))))
0b149f61 (4 1790696799682 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "The VS Code extension") (src . "") (parent . root) (ord . 12))))
c75b94f0 (5 1790696805860 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "Before you start") (src . "The extension drives the theourgia core installed on the machine. Install the core first (from source today; a Homebrew tap arrives with the 1.0 release), then configure the settings:\n\n| Setting | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `theourgia.corePath` | The directory holding the core (a checkout or a product directory). Required. |\n| `theourgia.libDirs` | Extra directories for `CHEZSCHEMELIBDIRS`, after `corePath`. |\n| `theourgia.store` | The store directory. Required. |\n| `theourgia.actor` | The name recorded with every write. Defaults to the OS user name. |\n| `theourgia.writer` | The draft space this window writes into. Defaults to the actor. |\n| `theourgia.scheme` | The Chez Scheme executable. Defaults to `scheme`. |\n| `theourgia.timeoutMs` | How long one request may take. Defaults to 30000. |") (parent . "d9l36a5r.4") (ord . 0))))
7c63db37 (6 1790696811503 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "Installing the extension") (src . "Install the `.vsix` package from the command line:\n\n```\ncode --install-extension theourgia-darwin-arm64-0.1.0.vsix\n```\n\nThe Visual Studio Marketplace listing arrives when the extension is published there.") (parent . "d9l36a5r.4") (ord . 1))))
351e6ae8 (7 1790696816897 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "What it does") (src . "An outline tree of the store appears in the side bar. Opening a node shows the blocks directly under it. A block opens as a markdown buffer with its heading and body.\n\nSaving writes a durable working draft first, then sends a commit carrying the block's version. If the baseline has moved since the draft was taken, the commit is refused and the refusal hands back the winner's content. A save whose answer is lost is kept and can be retried; the request id, cursor and body are recorded before the commit is sent.\n\nRight-clicking a node and choosing \"Open as Document\" composes the block and everything under it into one read-only markdown document. Each block's heading level is its depth under the opened block. The document is re-read from the store each time it is opened.\n\nThe tree has a second mode, Files, showing the directory tree that export would write. \"New File Here\" creates a document at that path. \"Move to Directory\" and \"Rename File\" write the block's path, guarded by its version: a block that changed after the listing is refused and the view refreshes.\n\nA text-mode code block opens as its source in the language its `lang` field names. \"Go to Definition\" asks the store's `whereis` which block defines a name. \"Suggest a Split\" asks the core where a source file on disk could be divided into blocks, using the editor's own symbols for the cuts.\n\nWhen a writer's log cannot be read, the outline shows every other writer's blocks and says which one is missing, the path and the reason. The conflict count, the search results and the status bar all carry the same note until every writer is readable again.") (parent . "d9l36a5r.4") (ord . 2))))
266a63d5 (8 1790696826154 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "Platforms") (src . "0.1.0 is packaged for macOS on Apple Silicon. The extension takes a file lock through a small native module built for the packaging machine. Packages for Intel macOS and for Linux (x86-64 and arm64) are built by the repository's GitHub Actions workflow, each on its own platform; one is published only when the unit suite has passed on every target against a real core. There is no Windows package.") (parent . "d9l36a5r.4") (ord . 3))))
127202a7 (9 1790696834528 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (set "8pniyrtk.1x" src ":root{--bg:#fbfaf7;--bg2:#f3f1ea;--panel:#f7f5ef;--line:#e4e0d5;--fg:#1c1b18;\n  --dim:#6a655c;--acc:#12b09c;--acc2:#0d8a7a;--gold:#9a6b12;--teal:#0f6f68;\n  --kw:#1a8f8f;--str:#0f6f3f;--com:#8a857a;--num:#8a4b12}\n*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}\nhtml{scroll-behavior:smooth}\nbody{background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);\n  font:16px/1.65 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\\\"Segoe UI\\\",Roboto,\\\"Helvetica Neue\\\",Arial,sans-serif;\n  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}\ncode,pre,.mono{font-family:ui-monospace,\\\"SF Mono\\\",SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,\\\"Liberation Mono\\\",monospace}\na{color:var(--acc2);text-decoration:none}\na:hover{text-decoration:underline}\n.wrap{max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}\n.narrow{max-width:760px}\nnav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:10;background:rgba(251,250,247,.88);\n  backdrop-filter:blur(8px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\nnav .wrap{display:flex;align-items:center;height:56px;gap:22px}\nnav .logo{font-weight:700;color:var(--fg);font-size:17px;letter-spacing:-.2px}\nnav .logo span{color:var(--acc);font-size:20px;vertical-align:-1px;display:inline-block;transform:rotate(21.77deg) skewX(-12deg)}\nnav .links{margin-left:auto;display:flex;gap:18px;font-size:14px}\nnav .links a{color:var(--dim)}\nnav .links a:hover{color:var(--fg);text-decoration:none}\nnav .links a.on{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\nheader{padding:80px 0 56px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;\n  background:radial-gradient(60% 50% at 50% 0%,#e4f4f4 0%,transparent 100%)}\nheader .wrap{position:relative;z-index:1}\n.glyph{font-size:44px;color:var(--acc);line-height:1;display:inline-block;transform:rotate(21.77deg) skewX(-12deg);font-weight:700}\nh1{font-size:54px;letter-spacing:-1.2px;margin:10px 0 16px}\n.tag{font-size:21px;color:var(--dim);max-width:660px;margin-bottom:12px}\n.tag b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\n.sub{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:30px}\n.cta{display:flex;gap:14px;margin-bottom:38px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.btn{display:inline-block;padding:11px 22px;border-radius:8px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600}\n.btn.primary{background:var(--acc);color:#fff}\n.btn.primary:hover{filter:brightness(1.12);text-decoration:none}\n.btn.ghost{border:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--fg)}\n.btn.ghost:hover{border-color:var(--dim);text-decoration:none}\nsection{padding:64px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.kicker{color:var(--acc);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase}\nh2{font-size:32px;margin:8px 0 14px;letter-spacing:-.5px}\nh3{font-size:21px;margin-bottom:10px}\np{margin-bottom:14px}\n.lead{color:var(--dim);font-size:17px;max-width:700px}\n.grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:36px;margin-top:36px}\n.grid2>*{min-width:0}\n.card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px 24px}\n.card h3{font-size:18px;margin-bottom:8px}\n.card p{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:0}\n.card p+p{margin-top:10px}\n.nums{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(170px,1fr));gap:1px;\n  background:var(--line);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:32px}\n.num{background:var(--bg);padding:20px}\n.num b{display:block;font-size:30px;letter-spacing:-.5px;color:var(--acc);margin-bottom:6px}\n.num span{color:var(--dim);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;display:block}\npre{background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px;\n  overflow-x:auto;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}\npre.wide{font-size:12.5px}\ncode{color:var(--acc);font-size:.86em;background:var(--bg2);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px}\npre code{background:none;padding:0;color:inherit;font-size:inherit}\n.k{color:var(--kw)}.s{color:var(--str)}.c{color:var(--com);font-style:italic}.n{color:var(--num)}\ntable{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-top:24px;font-size:14.5px}\nth,td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:9px 12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}\nth{background:var(--bg2);font-weight:600}\ntd.mono,th.mono{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap}\n.verb{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:16px 0}\n.verb:first-child{border-top:none}\n.verb .sig{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--fg);\n  background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:7px 10px;\n  display:block;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre}\n.verb .d{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-top:8px}\n.verb .r{float:right;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;\n  color:var(--dim);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:1px 6px;margin-left:8px}\n.note{border-left:3px solid var(--gold);background:#fdfaf2;padding:14px 18px;\n  border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin-top:24px;font-size:15px;color:var(--dim)}\n.note b{color:var(--fg)}\n.steps{counter-reset:s;margin-top:28px}\n.step{position:relative;padding-left:46px;margin-bottom:26px}\n.step:before{counter-increment:s;content:counter(s);position:absolute;left:0;top:-2px;\n  width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--acc);color:#fff;\n  font-size:14px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}\n.step h3{font-size:18px;margin-bottom:6px}\n.step p{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:0}\nfooter{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:40px 0;color:var(--dim);font-size:14px}\nfooter .wrap{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}\nfooter .sp{margin-left:auto}\n.diagram{margin-top:36px}\n.diagram svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}\n@media (max-width:760px){\n  h1{font-size:38px}\n  header{padding:56px 0 40px}\n  .tag{font-size:18px}\n  .grid2{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}\n  nav .wrap{gap:12px}\n  nav .links{gap:11px;font-size:12.5px}\n  section{padding:48px 0}\n  h2{font-size:26px}\n}\n.subsec{margin-top:38px}\n.subsec h3{font-size:20px;margin-bottom:10px}\n.subsec h4{font-size:16px;margin:24px 0 8px}\n.subsec p{color:var(--dim)}\n.subsec .lead{color:var(--dim)}\nol.design{margin:18px 0 0 22px;color:var(--dim)}\nol.design li{margin:10px 0}\nol.design li b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\nul.design{margin:18px 0 0 22px;color:var(--dim);list-style:none;padding:0}\nul.design li{margin:14px 0;padding-left:18px;border-left:3px solid var(--acc)}\nul.design li b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\n.md-body{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:56px 24px}\n.md-body h1{font-size:40px;letter-spacing:-1px;margin-bottom:8px}\n.md-body h2{font-size:28px;margin:44px 0 12px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.md-body h3{font-size:20px;margin:30px 0 8px}\n.md-body h4{font-size:16px;margin:22px 0 6px;color:var(--fg)}\n.md-body p{color:var(--dim);margin:0 0 14px}\n.md-body blockquote{margin:18px 0;padding:12px 18px;border-left:3px solid var(--gold);background:#fdfaf2;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0}\n.md-body blockquote p{margin:0}\n.md-body pre{margin:14px 0}\n.md-body code{color:var(--acc)}"))
3d03cc81 (10 1790696842104 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (del "8pniyrtk.8i"))
99f18ae9 (11 1790696842306 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . code) (mode . datum) (lang . chez) (body define (page-index) (shell "Theourgia -- a block-graph storage engine for LLM agents" "A knowledge base agents and people write into together: a minimal query surface, one graph across code and prose, backlinks in one query, deterministic context assembly, a shared editor, scratchpads with per-block optimistic commits, and Scheme blocks that run." "Home" (list (quasiquote (header (div (@ (class "wrap")) (div (@ (class "glyph")) "T") (h1 "Theourgia") (p (@ (class "tag")) (unquote (copy "Tagline"))) (p (@ (class "sub")) (unquote (copy "Hero sub"))) (div (@ (class "cta")) (a (@ (class "btn primary") (href "https://github.com/guenchi/theourgia")) "Get the code") (a (@ (class "btn ghost") (href "why.html")) "Why not markdown") (a (@ (class "btn ghost") (href "manual.html")) "The 32 verbs"))))) (sec "features" "Core features" "A Living Graph Engine" #f (prose "Core features lead")) (sec "query" "01" "A Minimal Query Surface for Agents" (copy "F1 lead") (code-of "F1 example")) (sec "graph" "02" "One Unified Graph Across Docs and Source Code" (copy "F2 lead") (graph-svg) (quasiquote (p (@ (style "margin-top:22px")) (a (@ (href "manual.html")) "The store, the block and the log, in full") " ->"))) (sec "refs" "03" "Global Backlinks at Near-Zero Cost" (copy "F3 lead") (code-of "Refs, verbatim") (prose "F3 measurement") (table-of "F3 cost table")) (sec "context" "04" "Deterministic Context Assembly" (copy "F4 lead") (prose "Context two layers") (ulist-of "Context sub-features")) (sec "people" "05" "Humans and Agents in the IDE" (copy "F5 lead") (ulist-of "IDE scarce uses")) (sec "concurrency" "06" "Zero-Conflict Concurrent Workspaces & Isolated Execution" (copy "F6 lead") (ulist-of "Concurrency sub-features") (code-of "A refusal, verbatim")) (sec "evaluate" "07" "A Lisp Machine: A Living Knowledge Base" (copy "F7 lead") (ulist-of "Lisp Machine sub-features") (code-of "History evaluation, verbatim") (quasiquote (p (@ (class "lead") (style "margin-top:18px")) "The definition was changed between the two calls. The second asks for the " "earlier cut and gets the behaviour that was there then."))) (sec "measured" "Measured" "Numbers, and where they came from" #f (nums-panel "Numbers") (note-of "How the numbers were taken")) (sec "start" "Start" "A store is a directory" #f (code-of "Quickstart") (quasiquote (p (@ (class "lead") (style "margin-top:22px")) (unquote (copy "Install")))))))) (doc . "") (parent . "8pniyrtk.2") (ord . 73))))
c47d9a1d (12 1790696848606 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (del "8pniyrtk.20"))
e807fe4a (13 1790696848817 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . code) (mode . datum) (lang . chez) (body define (topnav here) (define (lk href label) (if (equal? here label) (list (quote a) (list (quote @) (list (quote href) href) (list (quote class) "on")) label) (list (quote a) (list (quote @) (list (quote href) href)) label))) (quasiquote (nav (div (@ (class "wrap")) (div (@ (class "logo")) (a (@ (href "index.html") (style "color:inherit")) (span "T") " Theourgia")) (div (@ (class "links")) (unquote (lk "why.html" "Why")) (unquote (lk "manual.html" "Manual")) (unquote (lk "changelog.html" "Changelog")) (unquote (lk "agents.html" "Agents")) (a (@ (href "https://github.com/guenchi/theourgia")) "GitHub")))))) (doc . "") (parent . "8pniyrtk.2") (ord . 74))))
e34e0c14 (14 1790696855744 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (del "8pniyrtk.94"))
cb624d46 (15 1790696855947 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (put ((kind . code) (mode . datum) (lang . chez) (body define (manual-md) (join (list (md-head 1 "Theourgia manual") (md-head 2 "Installing") (md-para "Prerequisites") (md-head 3 "Homebrew") (md-para "Homebrew") (md-head 3 "npm") (md-para "npm") (md-head 3 "From source") (md-para "From source") (md-head 3 "Connecting a client") (md-para "Connecting a client") (md-head 2 "What a store is") (md-head 3 "A store") (md-para "A store") (md-fence "Store layout") (md-head 3 "A block") (md-para "A block") (md-fence "A block, as the store answers it") (md-head 3 "The log is the only truth") (md-para "The log is the only truth") (md-head 4 "Deletion keeps the history") (md-para "Deletion keeps the history") (md-head 3 "One graph over code and prose") (md-para "Everything is a block") (md-head 3 "One answer shape") (md-para "One answer shape") (md-head 3 "Writers") (md-para "A writer is an identity") (md-head 3 "Drafts, then commit") (md-para "Drafts, then commit") (md-head 4 "A refusal hands back the winner") (md-para "A refusal hands back the winner") (md-head 3 "One store per scope") (md-para "One store per scope") (md-head 3 "The daemon") (md-para "The daemon") (md-head 3 "Put the store in git") (md-para "Put the store in git") (md-head 4 "What to exclude, and what to keep") (md-fence "A store's gitignore") (md-head 4 "What a clone can do, and when") (md-fence "A clone's first write") (md-quote "What adopt does to a clone") (md-head 2 (join (list (number->string (length verb-table)) " verbs"))) (md-para "Reference intro") (md-verbs) (md-head 2 "Working with agents") (md-head 3 "The MCP shell") (md-para "The MCP shell") (md-head 3 "One writer per session") (md-para "One writer per session") (md-head 3 "One store per machine") (md-para "One store per machine") (md-head 3 "The memory recipe") (md-para "The memory recipe") (md-head 2 "The VS Code extension") (md-head 3 "Before you start") (md-para "Before you start") (md-head 3 "Installing the extension") (md-para "Installing the extension") (md-head 3 "What it does") (md-para "What it does") (md-head 3 "Platforms") (md-para "Platforms") (md-head 2 "Limits") (md-para "Limits")))) (doc . "") (parent . "8pniyrtk.2") (ord . 75))))
6e84ee77 (16 1790696893285 "guenchi" (("8pniyrtk" . 328)) (set "8pniyrtk.8n" src "Get a tagged tarball of Theourgia and place igropyr beside it under one library root:\n\n```\nlibrary-root/\n  theourgia/\n  igropyr/\n```\n\nCompile both into one output directory. On a Homebrew machine the interpreter is `chez`; the lines below say `scheme` for the upstream build.\n\n```\nscheme --script theourgia/build.ss library-root objects\n```\n\nThe three wrapper scripts -- `theourgia`, `theourgia-mcp`, and `theourgiad` -- expect `CHEZSCHEMELIBDIRS` set to the objects directory and `CHEZSCHEMELIBEXTS` set to `.so`.\n\nObjects start about twelve times faster than source (measured: 50 ms from objects, 572 ms from source). Never place them in the source tree -- a stale `.so` beside a `.sc` is resolved in preference to it."))
